A||||4||Doni Hagan||HIGH IDLE/HARD WARM STARTS?||||5||
Z||000000||Doni Hagan||07-16-2001||11:18 PM||||It's time to pick some brains... Recently, my 87GT w/auto tranny has been idling around 2000 when cold. It goes down after the car has warmed up but still idles high intermittently (1500 to 1000 in gear. Normal was about 750-800 when warm in gear. Also, when warm it's much harder to start. I've checked the EGR tube (no leaks) and ran for codes (none.) I was thinking it may be the ISC but like I said, no codes. I'd like to think the problem is something simpler and cheaper. A vacuum leak, perhaps?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Soelas||07-17-2001||12:40 AM||||I had the same type of idle problem with my '84. However, it didn't have hard warm starts. I replaced the Oxygen sensor (since the computer was giving me that code) and also replaced the EGR valve at that time (can't remember why I replaced it). The problem went away.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Doni Hagan||07-17-2001||09:28 AM||||Jeez, I'd hate to have to replace the O2 sensor just to find that the problem is still there. There's no code being set for it or anything else, for that matter. The EGR was replaced during the last tune up (about 9K ago.)<P>I'll pull one off my parts car and see if it makes a difference. ||||reg||6
Z||000003||The Fieromaster||07-17-2001||05:12 PM||||There are only a few things that could cause it...<P>Vaccum leak (check by the EGR valve that tube breaks allot) and checkk yout o2 sensor, the incomming air temp sensor (by the intake can), and the map sensor.. all are responsible for adjusting the fuel air mixture... if one is bad or sending bad readings it could cause high idle!<P>------------------<BR>      <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">        <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Doni Hagan||07-17-2001||07:32 PM||||Thanks, guys, for your advice. <P>I'll check the EGR, etc tomorrow night. That's the first chance I'll have to spend time with it. Someone else suggested I check the throttle cable for binding and the throttle body for dirt. I'm checkin' it all!||||reg||14
